Menu="AsustorControl:2"
Title="LEDs and Buttons"
Tag="lightbulb-o"
Markdown="false"
---
<div id="tab-leds">
    <div id="ac-leds-note" class="ac-banner ac-banner-warn" style="display:none"></div>

    <table class="tablesorter shift ups" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        <thead><tr><th>Bay</th><th>Disk</th><th>Activity LED</th><th>Fault LED</th><th>Locate</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="ac-bay-list"><tr><td colspan="5">Loading...</td></tr></tbody>
    </table>
    <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        <button onclick="locateBay(0)" class="ac-btn ac-btn-primary">Locate all bays (30 s)</button>
        <button onclick="locateBay('stop')" class="ac-btn">Stop locate</button>
        <span id="ac-front-status" style="margin-left:12px;"></span>
    </div>

    <dl>
        <dt>LED control:</dt>
        <dd><select id="cfg-leds-enabled"><option value="yes">Enabled</option><option value="no">Disabled (leave LEDs alone)</option></select></dd>
    </dl>
    <blockquote class="inline_help">Bay activity (blinks on disk I/O), bay fault (Unraid marks the disk disabled/invalid or with read errors) and the status LED (steady = array started, slow blink = parity check/rebuild, fast blink = array stopped; red = a disk is disabled, invalid or missing).</blockquote>
    <dl>
        <dt>Bay order:</dt>
        <dd><input type="text" id="cfg-bay-ports" size="20" placeholder="auto"></dd>
    </dl>
    <blockquote class="inline_help">auto = bay N is the Nth port of the ASM1166 SATA controller. If Locate lights the wrong bay, list the ATA port numbers in bay order, e.g. 2,1,3,4,5,6.</blockquote>
    <dl>
        <dt>USB Copy button, short press:</dt>
        <dd><select id="cfg-copy-short" class="ac-action"></select></dd>
    </dl>
    <dl>
        <dt>USB Copy button, long press:</dt>
        <dd><select id="cfg-copy-long" class="ac-action"></select></dd>
    </dl>
    <dl>
        <dt>Long press is at least:</dt>
        <dd><input type="number" id="cfg-long-press" min="1" max="30" size="3"> seconds</dd>
    </dl>
    <blockquote class="inline_help">log = Action Log entry; notify = Unraid notification; locate = blink every bay 30 s; script = run /boot/config/plugins/asustor-control/button-copy-short.sh or button-copy-long.sh. There is no built-in shutdown action. The power button is handled by Unraid (ACPI) as before.</blockquote>
    <dl>
        <dt>&nbsp;</dt>
        <dd><button onclick="saveLedConfig()" class="ac-btn ac-btn-primary">Apply</button> <span id="ac-buttons-last"></span></dd>
    </dl>

    <table class="tablesorter shift ups" style="margin:16px 0;">
        <thead><tr><th colspan="2">LED/button driver add-on</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td style="width:30%">This kernel</td><td id="ac-kmods-status">--</td></tr>
            <tr><td></td><td><button id="ac-kmods-install" onclick="kmodsInstall()" class="ac-btn ac-btn-primary">Install LED/button drivers</button>
                <span id="ac-kmods-result"></span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <blockquote class="inline_help">Unraid's kernel has no leds-gpio or gpio-keys-polled driver, so the LEDs and buttons the Asustor platform driver describes stay unused. The add-on installs those two drivers (plus LED blink triggers) built for exactly this Unraid kernel, and refuses on a kernel it has no build for.</blockquote>
</div>
